0..80 Comment "//! A case that prunes: an arm whose constructor cannot stand at the scrutinee\'s"
81..158 Comment "//! index is left out. Each branch of a case on an indexed family binds, past"
159..228 Comment "//! its fields, the path from the index its constructor states to the"
229..308 Comment "//! scrutinee\'s; a left-out arm eliminates that path, its two ends apart, which"
309..353 Comment "//! needs no rule beyond the case of no arms"
354..428 Comment "//! [Cockx-2016-unifiers_as_equivalences]. An arm whose ends are not apart"
429..486 Comment "//! cannot be left out; that is in the pathological twin."
487..490 Comment "//!"
491..541 Comment "//! - cites: [Cockx-2016-unifiers_as_equivalences]"
542..545 Comment "//!"
546..685 Comment "//! [Cockx-2016-unifiers_as_equivalences]: https://doi.org/10.1145/2951913.2951917 \"Cockx, Devriese and Piessens, Unifiers as equivalences\""
